# Byte-exact checkout.
#
# manifest.json records the SHA-256 of the exact bytes of every published file.
# Git's default `core.autocrlf` behaviour on Windows rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout, which changes those bytes and makes `tools/verify_manifest.py` report
# 329 spurious "CHANGED" files on Linux CI. That is line-ending drift, not
# tampering, and it is exactly the kind of false alarm that trains a reader to
# ignore the integrity check.
#
# `* -text` marks every path as binary for git's purposes: no end-of-line
# conversion in either direction, in either platform. The digests in
# manifest.json then mean the same thing everywhere.
#
# The same reasoning applies to the preserved curated deposit, which ships its own
# copy of this file at zenodo-deposit/.gitattributes. Its
# scripts/verify_historical_integrity.py has the same requirement.
* -text